# Generated files are owned by their generator, not by the formatter.
#
# ADR-006 §2 requires re-running the art scripts to be BYTE-IDENTICAL, so that
# any change to the art is an intentional git diff. A formatter that rewrites
# generated output breaks that guarantee outright: the generator writes one
# shape, `lint-staged` rewrites it on commit, and the next regeneration shows
# a diff that nobody made.
#
# This was found at the v0.5 RC — six `.anim.json` sidecars came back modified
# from a clean regeneration, and had been flip-flopping since the character
# generator started emitting them.

assets/src/**/*.anim.json

# Measurement artefacts, written by the E2E performance criteria. Same reason:
# the run that produces them owns their shape, and a formatter rewriting them
# means every measurement shows up as a diff against the last commit's
# formatting rather than against the last measurement.
docs/perf/*.json

# Build output and coverage reports.
assets/dist/
dist/
out/
coverage/
